data.content:
## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.OpenApi v2 (used by ASP.NET Core 10)

The underlying library upgraded from **OpenApi v1** → **v2**, targeting **OpenAPI 3.1**. Here's what broke and how to fix each piece:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed
OpenApi v2 uses `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead of the `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// ✅ New
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `OpenApiReference` + `ReferenceType` replaced by typed reference classes
Instead of a generic `OpenApiReference` with a `ReferenceType` enum, v2 has specific classes like `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference`, `OpenApiSchemaReference`, etc.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// ✅ New
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};
```

### 3. `Schema.Nullable` property removed
OpenAPI 3.1 models nullability via the `type` array. The `Nullable` bool is gone; use the `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag instead.

```csharp
// ❌ Old
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// ✅ New — remove the Null flag from the type
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

*(To **make** something nullable, you'd use `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`)*

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of changes

| What | Old (v1 / .NET 9) | New (v2 / .NET 10) |
|---|---|---|
| Value literals | `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, … | `JsonValue.Create(…)` / `JsonNode` |
| Schema nullability | `schema.Nullable = bool` | `schema.Type \|= JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| Security scheme ref | `OpenApiSecurityScheme` + `OpenApiReference` | `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")` |
| Namespace | `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` + `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References` |
